quran[9]{c,v,t}:
  39,32,"So, who is more unjust than the one who attributes lies to Allah and denies the truth when it comes to him? Is not the final abode of the disbelievers in Hell?"
  39,33,The one who has brought the truth and the one who has confirmed it—they are the ones who are (truly) God-conscious.
  39,34,They shall have whatever they desire in the presence of their Lord. That is the reward of the virtuously excellent.
  39,35,(It is) so that Allah may absolve them of the worst of what they did and reward them with the best of what they used to do.
  39,36,Is Allah not sufficient for His servant? Yet they (the disbelievers) seek to frighten you (Esteemed Prophet) with those (false gods) besides Him! But whoever Allah leaves to stray will be left with no guide.
  39,37,"And whoever Allah guides, none can lead him astray. Is Allah not All-Mighty, Capable of Vengeance?"
  39,38,"If you ask them who created the heavens and the earth, they will surely say: ‘Allah’. Say: ‘Have you considered whatever (idols) you worship besides Allah? If Allah desires (some) harm for me, can they remove His harm? Or if He desires (some) mercy for me, can they withhold His mercy?’ Say: ‘Allah is Sufficient for me. In Him alone, the trusting people should put their trust.’"
  39,39,"(Esteemed Prophet!) Say: ‘My people! Act according to your position and ability, (for) I (too) am acting (according to mine). You will soon come to know,"
  39,40,"who is the one whom the punishment will overtake (in this life), which will disgrace him, and upon whom an everlasting torment (of the next life) will descend.’"
